      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T22:44:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think, macro allows for more natural expression of an interface method call—it looks like a normal call, for example `mStream-\u003esetHwVolume(volumes)`, just wrapped into a macro. Whereas, with a template we have to provide separately the object, the method, and the arguments: `serializeCall(mStream, IStreamOut::setHwVolume, volumes)`. This looks much less natural. With our use case we don\u0027t run into any limitations of macro parameters parsing. I do not really see much benefit from using the template implementation over a macro here. Shunkai, do you still think use of template code is preferred?",
      "parentUuid": "23857e01_972276a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "3218725962e79ad9520b8293d0f11b7fa77ca928",
